  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connect for Growth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kosovo):  .The Kosovo buy-in into the regional Connect for Growth (C4G).activity provides targeted assistance to maintain self-reliant electricity.supplies and avoid blackouts during the peak-load seasons due the high prices.of energy imports. The activity provides procurement advisory support to the.Kosovo Energy Corporation (KEK), as they seek services, supplies, and equipment.for repair and maintenance of generation and auxiliary assets necessary to.maintain domestic power generation and protect operational safety. To date, C4G.built the capacity and assisted KEK professional staff prepare a comprehensive.tender package for Unit A3 of the Kosovo A power plant. This includes drafting.prequalification documents, tender response templates, and detailed technical.specifications. Additionally, a thorough financial analysis was developed that.provided two options for Unit A3--either modernization or rehabilitation..In early November, the KEK technical committee decided to proceed with the.rehabilitation option. The estimated budget of &amp;euro;137.0 million is expected to be.approved as part of KEK&apos;s overall budget during the KEK Board&apos;s meeting.scheduled for the end of November. Thus, with FY 2024 funds, the activity will.build on the groundwork completed to date by supporting KEK to successfully.implement the tender and provide further technical assistance to improve its.procurement performance, enhance the reliability of its assets and apply.utility operations best practices. The activity aligns with JRS Goal 2 by.promoting U.S. energy options and increasing Kosovo&apos;s energy independence and.security. The activity also contributes to ICS Objective 3.2 by strengthening.Kosovo&apos;s commitment to a diverse and secure energy supply. This activity also.aligns with CAATSA Goal 7 supporting energy security through technical advice.and assistance designed to address energy vulnerabilities and increase energy.security... ..</narrative>
  </description>
